{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts","id":1564132,"title":"Spirit broods/Incarna for Breed Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-09-16T15:41:41-07:00","id":1564132,"title":"Spirit broods/Incarna for Breed Gifts","content":"I have said on other threads that I am a big believer of using spirit broods as a tool for the ST. It provides STs an organization that can make running the Umbra easier.<br /> <br /> One of the things broods do is explain why certain spirits teach what Gifts. It\u2019s not that Gifts are limited to only certain broods. Gift descriptions often given multiple types of spirits who teach that Gift, and the same Gift is often included on multiple lists (Sense Wyrm, for example, is on the list for Metis, Theurge, Black Furies, Silent Strider and Uktena lists in W20, and can be supposedly taught by any Gaian spirit). It\u2019s just that many spirit broods have \u201cauthorization \u201cto teach the same Gift. Spirit broods are an easy way to explain why certain Gifts are on the list for one\u2019s auspice, breed, and tribe.<br /> <br /> However, spirit broods have Incarna. So I would like to identify the various Gift teaching broods (of one\u2019s auspice, breed, and tribe) to an Incarna. (If you don't care about such things, I understand.)<br /> <br /> The Tribal Gifts are the easiest to explain. We know there are tribal totems for each other them that have their own spirit broods. Auspice Gifts are also easy. Auspice is determined by the Celestine Luna, and she ultimately is the one who decides which Gifts can be taught \u201cin class\u201d to each auspice. If we don\u2019t want to ultimately direct all auspices to Luna herself (or perhaps the Incarna Phoebe), then we can \u201cinvent\u201d Incarna for each of the moon phases. No matter what one decides, we can quickly move on.<br /> <br /> The Breed Gifts don\u2019t have such an obvious patron though. Presumably the Wolf Incarna (under whatever name) is the ultimate patron for the Lupus Gifts. Or perhaps as aspect of Wolf like Old Wolf of the Woods if we don\u2019t want Wolf himself to favor any one breed over another. That is easy to figure out. However, we don\u2019t have obvious patrons for the Homid and Metis Gifts.<br /> <br /> W20 does say that many homid breed Gifts are taught by ancestor spirits than nature spirits because humans have become strangers to the world of spirit. In lieu of a \u201cMan\u201d spirit, perhaps there\u2019s some kind of \u201cFirst Homid\u201d ancestor spirit out there that is effectively the patron for all homids. This paramount homid spirit doesn\u2019t necessarily need to be the ancestor spirit of the first ever homid Garou. just an important early one. Although I do think such a figure should pre-date all the tribes, and likely pre-dates the Pact. However, normally ancestor spirits don\u2019t increase in power to become an Incarna. The only examples we have are Black Spiral Dancers who have done that (Number Two and Hakaken). That\u2019s not good precedent. So perhaps its more like a City Father type figure (an Epiphling) that is like a \u201cMan As Tool Maker\u201d or something. If there\u2019s a Patriarch, why can\u2019t there be a Toolmaker, Lawgiver, Firebringer (or Firestarter), Namegiver, Tamer, or equivalent?<br /> <br /> The W20 description for Metis Gifts is more interesting. It says Metis Gifts tend to be an eclectic collection of \u201cpacts\u201d and powers. Since they are scorned, metis have learned to make friends where they can and take what allies they can get. This implies that perhaps originally metis Garou did not have a ready list of Gifts for their breed. After all, the metis are not \u201cnatural\u201d in the sense there\u2019s already an existing spirit that embodies the concept. Metis only emerged later.<br /> <br /> There is a creature in the Books of the Wyrm called the First Metis, but I extremely doubt that he should be a patron whose spirit brood is responsible for the Metis breed Gifts. It just creates too many problems for the setting.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that only gradually did metis form a list of Breed Gifts through individual metis actively making pacts, not just for themselves but for their entire breed. As these individual pacts accumulated, eventually one spirit gained enough power to collect, organize, and protect this eclectic group of spirits. Maybe Father Mule who would also be the pack totem described in Children of Gaia Tribebook, Revised? Since mules don\u2019t seem to have existed until 3500 BC at the earliest, the spirit would likely not exist until then, meaning a comprehensive breed list of Gifts available to all metis might not have existed until well into human history, perhaps not until the Classical Age.<br /> <br /> Those are my initial thoughts. Does anyone else have an opinion? Interested in comparing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-16T16:17:08-07:00","id":1564133,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea. And I definitely agree with you about the First M\u00e9tis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T11:32:25-07:00","id":1564142,"title":"","content":"This wouldn't change the multi-part &quot;authorization&quot; of spirit broods, since breeds and auspices still have a rather variable selection of spirits that teach the Gift. Spirit of the Fray, for instance, is taught by a cat-spirit; Cocoon, meanwhile, can be taught by insect-spirits or Weaver spirits. Lupus Gifts include both Monkey Tail and Catfeet. It seems like every one of them is cutting across brood lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564133#post1564133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea. And I definitely agree with you about the First M\u00e9tis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per A World of Rage p7, the Garou breed does <u>not</u> have an accent mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-17T12:01:41-07:00","id":1564143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564142#post1564142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This wouldn't change the multi-part &quot;authorization&quot; of spirit broods, since breeds and auspices still have a rather variable selection of spirits that teach the Gift. Spirit of the Fray, for instance, is taught by a cat-spirit; Cocoon, meanwhile, can be taught by insect-spirits or Weaver spirits. Lupus Gifts include both Monkey Tail and Catfeet. It seems like every one of them is cutting across brood lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Per A World of Rage p7, the Garou breed does <u>not</u> have an accent mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! Autocorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-22T23:23:40-07:00","id":1564290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564133#post1564133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea. And I definitely agree with you about the First M\u00e9tis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think a &quot;Father Mule&quot; Incarna is a good patron for the metis breed? How about a &quot;Firebringer&quot; for the homid breed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T04:12:39-07:00","id":1564294,"title":"","content":"Mule sounds insulting, so probably not. Firebringer could work though.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I can\u2019t tell if you\u2019re being sarcastic or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T06:36:42-07:00","id":1564298,"title":"","content":"Mule seems right to me because owning the insult is the point.<br /> <br /> In one go you use the animal, recognize the concept/theme behind the Metis Breed and take ownership of it to turn into a source of power.<br /> <br /> But it would require careful thought on the spirit, because it would make or break the idea. If Father Mule reflects prejudice against mixed people, even if/especially as a joke, that will be offensive as hell. It does work as someone that uses the lived experience of being mixed and the prejudice it entails as empowerment.<br /> <br /> Now I'm curious, how bad is it to be mixed in the US at different states? And how much does it vary through the world? I know it's particularly bad in South Africa and Japan, and it really is secondary in Brazil (we give little attention to notions of purity compared to your actual appearance).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T13:17:45-07:00","id":1564307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564290#post1564290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you think a &quot;Father Mule&quot; Incarna is a good patron for the metis breed? How about a &quot;Firebringer&quot; for the homid breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d have suggested something like \u2018Brother Mule\u2019 or \u2018Uncle Mule\u2019 to keep the counterculture, rebellious aspects of calling on this spirit quite clear (Metis want a friend to help them out of a bad place, not another master).<br /> <br /> This is, I admit, promoted by fond memories of reading THE TALES OF UNCLE REMUS as a youngster (and \u2018Brother Mule\u2019 works for both a Medieval or a more modern setting, when you remember the example of Saint Francis of Assisi).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T14:02:31-07:00","id":1564312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564294#post1564294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mule sounds insulting, so probably not. Firebringer could work though.<br /> <br /> Sorry. I can\u2019t tell if you\u2019re being sarcastic or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not being sarcastic. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Father_Mule\" target=\"_blank\">Father Mule</a> (specific name, not just &quot;Mule&quot;) is an existing canonical pack totem. It is described in the revised Children of Gaia Tribebook. It is a Totem of Respect. He's described as the sterile son of Horse, and that he is particularly fond of metis. Lupus and Homids, in general, don't like the totem for their own reasons. Father Mule will not accept pack members who are &quot;fertile&quot;. That's not just metis, as both men and women homids and lupus can be infertile for whatever reasons. They might be infertile through a genetic disorder, medical issue, injury, or naturally barren for whatever reason; and homid women can be post-menopausal. All would fit the definition of not being fertile. However, I think in the main, Father Mule will be a totem to packs that are all metis except for a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> There's not many existing pack totems that are clearly associated with metis, and thus there are few existing candidates that make sense as a potential Incarna master of its own spirit brood that provides breed gifts to Metis. In fact, it's the only one I remember that clearly favors metis.<br /> <br /> Not all hybrids are infertile, but many are. That's why I think a sterile hybrid like a mule would be appropriate for metis since they are naturally sterile as well. Furthermore, people find mules useful. While some hybrids are noticeably inferior than either lineage, mules possess hybrid vigor and display improved traits over their parents. People purposefully breed mules because they are hardier and live longer than horses, and are more intelligent than donkeys. They are also more cooperative and patient in temperament. It is rare for mules to become pregnant, but it has happened. However, rather than being a detriment, I think that might provide even more enthusiasm of metis for the totem.<br /> <br /> Humans associate a lot of positive traits to mules. People who have them care just as much for them as they do their horses and donkeys (or other animals). So that could explain why Father Mule had enough spiritual strength to attract lesser spirits to itself for protection. It could then proceed to gather spirits around it for protection, and many spirits who were already providing some Gifts to metis would be inclined to join it.<br /> <br /> So even when I considered non-canonical spirits as candidates for a patron of the metis breed Gifts, I haven't come up with a better candidate than Father Mule. I would love to hear suggestions though.<br /> <br /> The spirit brood of Father Mule would likely be limited, but that's OK. Not all spirit broods will be as large as Stag's. It'll include a lot of metis Ancestor Spirits, lesser mule spirits, the spirits of other sterile or low-producing hybrids, and other oddball spirits. The description of the Father Mule pack totem says that Garou who follow the Horse or Bull pack totem are well disposed to Father Mule, so those spirits of domesticated animals are well disposed to him. So while he may not have all animals spirits of horses, bulls, donkeys, etc., he may have some specific variety of such spirits in his brood (in the same way that multiple spirit broods have a Raven spirit in them). Probably quite a few pack animal versions of the spirits (camels, yaks, goats, llamas, etc.) may be included in the brood.<br /> <br /> After reviewing the W20 corebook's metis breed gifts, I see there are some elemental spirits, various animal spirits (rats, lizards, snakes, moles, wolves, chameleons, octopi, cats, birds, turtles, porcupines, spiders, venomous creatures), some epiphlings (spirits of hate, intellect, fury, trickery, madness), Lunes, and Chimmerlings. So if we assume that while such spirits outside this breed gift brood can also teach these Gifts, that Father Mule must have attracted a wide variety of (renegade/orphaned/lost) spirits to it. Personally, I assume that there was likely a concerted effort by many of the greatest ranked metis to win chiminage of some powerful jagglings or even lesser incarna to provide gifts to the Metis breed, and some of these ended up joining the brood of Father Mule. We're also told that the fifth level Totem Gift is taught directly by the Tribal Totem, but that is obviously a favor provided to the metis separate from any spirit brood that provides the other Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 09-24-2026, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-23T14:04:37-07:00","id":1564313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564307#post1564307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d have suggested something like \u2018Brother Mule\u2019 or \u2018Uncle Mule\u2019 to keep the counterculture, rebellious aspects of calling on this spirit quite clear (Metis want a friend to help them out of a bad place, not another master).</div> </div> </div> </div>I just used the canonical name as included in the revised Children of Gaia Tribebook. If people want to use the concept, but change the name to just Mule or select some other title, I don't think it changes anything. So people can use whatever they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-07T11:44:37-07:00","id":1564587,"title":"","content":"An entirely fair point.- I vaguely recalled that Mule had been a totem, but could not remember the exact name given.\ud83d\ude42","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-11T12:53:44-07:00","id":1564692,"title":"","content":"For the ur-Homid ancestor spirit you could also perhaps do something similar to Wolf where, even if we want \u2018Human\u2019 or \u2018Wolf\u2019 itself to be beyond the range of contact, we could have \u2018Old Man of the Field\u2019 or something as the counterpart to Old Wolf of the Wood. One snag could be deciding whether or not the ur-homid brood-master should be specifically an ur-ancestor for human-born garou or a pan-human ur-ancestor type spirit. The big minefield is probably going to be whether or not these spirits have or can share accurate information about the origins of the Garou (and other changing breeds). For the sake of ease, one may want to avoid this by saying that the stories told are contradictory or that the ur-ancestor spirits don\u2019t discuss such matters anymore (for whatever reason). <br /> <br /> I do also like Firemaker as an option for a humano-centric spirit, kind of has Prometheus vibes and there\u2019s plenty of stories around the world of fire-stealing heroes (although many of these heroes aren\u2019t actually human and thus perhaps the Firebringer fits more as a non-human patron of humanity). I could also see something like Old Teacher working as a catch-all for law-givers and tool-makers and various other legendary figures who teach hunting, weaving, agriculture, horticulture, writing, etc. (perhaps Old Teacher or Firemaker ought to also have some ties to Mages altho that\u2019s not really our priority here of course). <br /> <br /> For the Garou-born, maybe if one wants a precursor to Father Mule, one could lean into the angle of the breed being unwanted and despised and have something like Foundling, a spirit born from things like infant exposure and bastardy, as an original brood leader (what Gryphon is to extinct and monstrous beasts, Foundling is to abandoned things). Various spirits who are on the outs with their original broods then might serve as a catch-all from which the garou-born can derive their pacts once they enter Foundling\u2019s sphere of influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-12T12:20:13-07:00","id":1564706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564692#post1564692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do also like Firemaker as an option for a humano-centric spirit, kind of has Prometheus vibes and there\u2019s plenty of stories around the world of fire-stealing heroes (although many of these heroes aren\u2019t actually human and thus perhaps the Firebringer fits more as a non-human patron of humanity). I could also see something like Old Teacher working as a catch-all for law-givers and tool-makers and various other legendary figures who teach hunting, weaving, agriculture, horticulture, writing, etc. (perhaps Old Teacher or Firemaker ought to also have some ties to Mages altho that\u2019s not really our priority here of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are definitely multiple candidates an ST can use to be the patron of homid gifts. I personally like Firebringer the best because of those Prometheus vibes. Very mythical. Mastery of fire is also something that happened way in the distant past (unlike many other human cultural achievements). Behaviorally modern humans are around 50,000 years old, and anatomically modern humans around 200,000 years old. But archaic humans using fire is probably around 400,000 years old. So it predates lots of other things that distinguish humans from animals (or modern humans in general). There's also various lore in Werewolf that indicates the importance Garou hold on that. Besides the actual Master of Fire homid gift, the Red Talon legend included in the first Werewolf Players Guide also makes use of it.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's necessary to specifically define what kind of spirit the Firebringer is. Incarna aren't usually willing to communicate with lesser beings, and even those who do tend to be enigmatic and distant. All that is needed to be &quot;known&quot; is that it's the spirit considered to have been involved in mankind's learning how to control fire. Keep it mythic. Let players speculate however they want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564692#post1564692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Garou-born, maybe if one wants a precursor to Father Mule, one could lean into the angle of the breed being unwanted and despised and have something like Foundling, a spirit born from things like infant exposure and bastardy, as an original brood leader (what Gryphon is to extinct and monstrous beasts, Foundling is to abandoned things). Various spirits who are on the outs with their original broods then might serve as a catch-all from which the garou-born can derive their pacts once they enter Foundling\u2019s sphere of influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea of a Foundling spirit! I'll need to include that in the brood. However, I think it's perhaps too humanocentric to be ideal for the metis. It's not that animals don't abandon their offspring for whatever reason, it's that only humans seem to think that's a bad thing (probably because unlike many animals, humans take a lot longer postbirth to look out for themselves) and not until civilization became advanced enough that there was enough of a surplus to take care of foundlings. Again, nothing wrong with the idea for the spirit. I like it, but personally I wouldn't consider it an earlier candidate than Mule as a spirit that can serve the role of the brood's protector. But like all discussions of this kind, STs will always do what they like best.<br /> <br /> I do agree that lots of orphaned spirits might gravitate to this metis patron brood. Many spirits on the outs with their original broods can likely find some other Incarna to take them in, but this is a good brood for the really misfit spirits that can't find anywhere else to go. You just need to create a few example jagglings of whatever spirit type and give it a name and background that explains its misfit nature that caused them to either be expelled from their original brood, or why they wanted to join this one. Good way to provide more personality to the brood if the ST considers that a good use of their time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-21T04:38:19-07:00","id":1564889,"title":"","content":"Wouldn\u2019t the most obvious teacher spirits for Breed gifts not be Ancestor Spirits? (At least for the Homid and Lupus breeds).<br /> <br /> After all, who else would be a more logical choice than the very progenitors of your bloodline? (One could also make it plain that these spirits are passing down lore that was passed down to them by their own ancestors to help make plain how old Garou society is and how important deep connection to their roots is to a Garou).<br /> <br /> That this leaves \u2018Metis\u2019 at the mercy of their ability to persuade ancestors to overlook the Litany in their favour (and very possibly doomed to fail) would make a good opportunity for roleplaying, as well as furnish a way to show that Ancestor Spirits are neither a purely benevolent influence nor any more inclined to march in philosophical lockstep than any Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-22T21:34:18-07:00","id":1564922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1564132-spirit-broods-incarna-for-breed-gifts?p=1564889#post1564889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn\u2019t the most obvious teacher spirits for Breed gifts not be Ancestor Spirits? (At least for the Homid and Lupus breeds).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancestor spirits are certainly an important part of the brood, and many Gifts explicitly name them as an example spirit that can teach certain Gifts.<br /> <br /> However, I rejected the idea that an Ancestor spirit would be the head of the spirit brood because we don't have examples of Gaian aligned Ancestor spirits/Garou who are Incarna (I belive the only two canon examples of Garou becoming Incarna are aligned with the Wyrm - Number Two of Malfeas and Hakaken). I briefly discussed this in the first post. So I went<br /> <br /> However, I'm not completely against the idea that there could be a &quot;First Homid&quot; or &quot;First Lupus&quot; ancestor spirit who does head the brood. It's something I could accept in someone else's chronicle as an explanation. However, I hope that the ST would put in some real effort to create a flavorful and mythic spirit (and one that hopefully predates the tribes so all Garou can equally claim it).<br /> <br /> I think there have been a few canon short stories set in that mythic past. I would check them first to see if I could find an example NPC that could fit.<br /> <br /> In fact, before I posted the thread, I did the check one short story I know of (Sam Chupp's The Night Flyer in Drums Around the Flyer (1994)), but decided I didn't think any of the characters in that story really fit the idea of an Incarna patron of one of the breeds. I also quickly checked my copy of the 1e Umbra: the Velvet Shadow to see if they mentioned any Ancestor spirits who were Incarna, but I couldn't find any. So that's why I looked at other existing spirits who could serve as good patrons for a brood that taught breed Gifts.<br /> <br /> At some point though, I eventually hope to create some interesting Ancestor spirit jagglings from that mythic time who assist the Incarna of these broods plus some other spirits in the fashion of the tribal brood spirits included in Axis Mundi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}